  "decision_gate": {
    "determination": "STRUCTURE RETENTION IMPROVES EVIDENCE RECALL",
    "justification": "Markdown table representation preserves substantially more answer-bearing evidence at a measured and acceptable token cost. Under the identical table selection threshold as Condition B (theta=2.0), GFM Markdown table retention jumps answer recall from 31.0% to 54.0% (+23.0 pp) and recovers 27 of 47 Stage C regressions (57.4% vs 6.4% in baseline B), while consuming only 227.9 mean tokens (-63.2% below Condition A). When threshold relaxation (theta=0.0) is applied, table evidence recall reaches 100% of table-bearing cases, completely resolving all 26 deep row truncation failures identified in Probe D.1."
  }
